WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.653
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:14.590
Unit twenty: Writing Under Exam Time. Today you will plan and write well in a limited time.

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.461
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.447
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.377
Time limit.

7
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:26.754
Time limit means the most time you are allowed.

8
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.605
There is a time limit of 40 minutes.

9
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:32.962
Your turn. Say: Time limit.

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.766
Time limit.

11
00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:38.320
Plan.

12
00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:41.537
Plan means to decide what you will do.

13
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.476
Plan before you write.

14
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:46.306
Your turn. Say: Plan.

15
00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:49.994
Plan.

16
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.600
Question.

17
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:54.906
Question means what you are asked to answer.

18
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:57.075
Read the question carefully.

19
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.045
Your turn. Say: Question.

20
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.808
Question.

21
00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.412
Task.

22
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:08.439
Task means a piece of work to do.

23
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.678
Read the task twice.

24
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.587
Your turn. Say: Task.

25
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:17.388
Task.

26
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.151
Word count.

27
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.324
Word count means the number of words.

28
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:24.254
Check the word count.

29
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.572
Your turn. Say: Word count.

30
00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:31.551
Word count.

31
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.480
Prioritise.

32
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:37.679
Prioritise means to do the most important things first.

33
00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:40.155
Prioritise the main points.

34
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.785
Your turn. Say: Prioritise.

35
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:48.052
Prioritise.

36
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:49.678
Manage.

37
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:53.066
Manage means to control or organise.

38
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.174
Manage your time well.

39
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:58.099
Your turn. Say: Manage.

40
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:01.969
Manage.

41
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:03.613
Review.

42
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.303
Review means to look at again.

43
00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:08.545
Review your answer at the end.

44
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.663
Your turn. Say: Review.

45
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.431
Review.

46
00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:19.745
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:23.314
Visal, how can I write well in an exam?

48
00:02:24.417 --> 00:02:33.640
Read the question carefully and underline the key words. Plan for three or four minutes, then write, and keep five minutes to check.

49
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.355
How do I plan quickly?

50
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:44.955
Write the main points in a short list and put them in order. A short plan keeps your essay clear and saves time.

51
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.539
What about the word count?

52
00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:56.158
Write at least the minimum words. Do not repeat yourself. Quality and organisation matter more than length.

53
00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.172
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:00.017 --> 00:03:02.887
Grammar focus: Time plan with will.

55
00:03:03.187 --> 00:03:04.699
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:07.360
I will plan for four minutes.

57
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.342
I will check my answer at the end.

58
00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.937
Use will plus the base verb to make a plan for your exam time.

59
00:03:15.683 --> 00:03:19.555
Be careful! Don't say: I will to plan for four minutes.

60
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.767
Say: I will plan for four minutes.

61
00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.416
No to after will.

62
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.038
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:31.101
Exam Day.

64
00:03:31.401 --> 00:03:34.307
Sreyneang has forty minutes for her writing task.

65
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.565
She reads the question twice and underlines key words.

66
00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.402
She plans for four minutes and writes her main points.

67
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.806
She writes steadily and watches the clock.

68
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.345
She keeps five minutes to review her answer.

69
00:03:50.433 --> 00:03:54.563
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:55.417 --> 00:03:57.927
A time limit is the most time blank allowed.

71
00:03:58.227 --> 00:04:01.695
A, you want. B, you pay. C, you are.

72
00:04:05.233 --> 00:04:07.477
The answer is C: you are.

73
00:04:08.617 --> 00:04:10.407
First, read the blank carefully.

74
00:04:10.707 --> 00:04:13.908
A, question. B, menu. C, map.

75
00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.431
The answer is A: question.

76
00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:22.769
A short plan keeps the essay blank.

77
00:04:23.069 --> 00:04:25.956
A, dark. B, clear. C, wet.

78
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.558
The answer is B: clear.

79
00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:35.413
Prioritise means do the blank things first.

80
00:04:35.713 --> 00:04:39.250
A, easy. B, last. C, important.

81
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.533
The answer is C: important.

82
00:04:45.683 --> 00:04:48.112
Sreyneang keeps five minutes to blank.

83
00:04:48.412 --> 00:04:51.671
A, review. B, sleep. C, shop.

84
00:04:55.233 --> 00:04:57.140
The answer is A: review.

85
00:04:58.333 --> 00:05:01.334
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:02.183 --> 00:05:04.612
How do you manage time in a writing exam?

87
00:05:13.417 --> 00:05:15.114
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:25.732
I read the question carefully and plan for a few minutes. I write the main points in order and watch the clock. I keep the last five minutes to review my answer.

89
00:05:26.032 --> 00:05:27.718
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:28.617 --> 00:05:32.790
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and time plan with will.

91
00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:37.716
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:05:38.016 --> 00:05:44.038
Congratulations! You have finished Online Writing Skills. See you in Online more new courses soon!

93
00:05:44.338 --> 00:05:47.826
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

